// The one construction shape whose missing instantiation is still a RUN-TIME abort, pinned here so
// the shared abort message stays exercised now that the constructor-call route is a check-time
// error (`class_type_param_unknown_instantiation.noe`).
//
// A **direct object literal** of a generic class, written outside the class, whose type parameter
// no field determines: `Repo { tbl: "x" }` says nothing about `T` — `T` appears in no field type —
// so the literal types as a bare `Repo` with no arguments and nothing is tagged.
//
// It is a different path from the constructor call this arc closed (`note_construction` on a
// literal, not `note_constructor_call` on a call), and it is not the same judgement either: the
// *same* literal inside `fn new` is erased ON PURPOSE (its `T` is a parameter, resolved one frame
// up by the call), so the erasure cannot simply be made an error where it is written. Closing it
// belongs with the literal's own inference, not here.
// expect: error E0058 at 20:33
// expect: exit 1
class Repo<T> {
    pub tbl: string

    fn model(): string {
        return self.tbl ~ ":" ~ type_name::<T>();
    }
}
r = Repo { tbl: "x" };
echo r.model();
